From 58dfb71ceedbf00678622c6b2b45b1d3428a9eab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:53:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/32] fix(desktop): shell-root safe-area inset +
 fixed-surface calc tops + toolbar/tab clearance

F4b: [data-contrib-shell] becomes the single in-flow padding site for
--safe-top (titlebar band, tree, and drawer containing block shift below
the notch together; popout shell intentionally included); the drawers'
and titlebar-chrome's own padding rules are removed to avoid
double-counting. Fixed surfaces add var(--safe-top) to their top calcs:
the three titlebar clusters, notifications, find-bar, overlay-view top
inset, and floating-pane viewport clamp.

F4e: the main transcript's top pad becomes
max(var(--titlebar-height)-0.5rem, 0px) + var(--chat-top-gap) so the
coarse-gated 6px gap (fine pointer: 0px, pixel-identical) survives the
CSS negative-padding clamp the raw expression used to hit.

User addendum A: coarse pointers get a 23px margin above zone tab strips
(cluster bottom 49 + 8px breathing room - titlebar band 34), keeping
44px toolbar targets clear of the first clickable tab row.
